  "limitations": "Planar Cartesian [x, y] only; no geodesic distance, 3D points, topology preservation or self-intersection repair. Tolerance is a perpendicular distance in input units (squared internally). At most 5000 points. Radial pre-filter (default) can give a different result from pure Douglas-Peucker; set highest_quality=true for the pure algorithm. Points with two or fewer entries are returned unchanged.",
  "port_notes": "Port of simplify.js (getSqDist, getSqSegDist, simplifyRadialDist, simplifyDPStep, simplifyDouglasPeucker, simplify) at the pinned commit. The recursive DP step is replaced by an explicit stack that emits indices in the identical in-order sequence, avoiding Python recursion limits. Object identity in the radial filter (prevPoint !== point) is replaced by index comparison. Default tolerance 1 and the strict greater-than comparisons are kept. Points are [x, y] arrays instead of {x, y} objects; kept_indices are added.",
